/target

# The template application is outside the workspace on purpose — see the root `Cargo.toml`'s
# `exclude` — so it has a `target/` and a lock file of its own. Neither is worth committing: the
# crate exists to be linted and copied, `cargo deny` does not see it, and a second lock file in the
# tree is a second thing to keep current for no benefit.
/examples/app-template/target
/examples/app-template/Cargo.lock

.claude/

# JetBrains project files. `.idea/workspace.xml` was committed once by accident (fd8ad06) and is
# untracked again here: it holds window layout, open tabs, run configurations and the cursor's last
# position, so every IDE session dirties it and no two developers ever want each other's copy.
.idea/

# The comparative suite (`compare/`) is a detached workspace with a lock file and a target directory
# of its own, and one arm has a Python virtual environment. The lock file **is** committed — the
# arms pin exact versions and a lock is what makes the pin reproducible — but nothing built is.
/compare/target
/compare/arms/textual/.venv
/compare/arms/notcurses/arm
